    "title": "Santa brings early Christmas joy to Houston's Third Ward at free toy giveaway - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brett Coomer ,\n1 days ago Michael Brooks, dressed as Santa, welcomes kids as they arrive to receive gifts during the 4th Annual Free Christmas Eve Family Festival and Toy Giveaway at The Savoy in Third Ward in Houston, Wednesday, Dec. 24, 2025. The festival featured Santa, more than 1,000 toys for kids, shoes a snow-covered sledding hill and music, helping ensure all children leave with a gift on Christmas Eve. (Brett Coomer/Houston Chronicle) Santa made an early stop in Houston’s Third Ward on Christmas Eve, greeting families at the 4th Annual Free Christmas Eve Family Festival and Toy Giveaway at The Savoy. More than 1,000 toys were handed out as children lined up to meet Santa, climb a snow-covered sledding hill — in Houston, no less — and dance to music filling the hall. The celebration turned The Savoy into a pocket of holiday magic, ensuring every child went home with a gift in hand and Christmas joy already well underway. These moments were captured by Houston Chronicle staff photographer Brett Coomer.\nSign up for Houston Chronicle newsletters here\nRead the original article on houstonchronicle.com\n32",
